  <p>
    I'm Wade Minter, and I live at the intersection of technology, sports, and performance. By day, I'm founder and COO of <a href="https://suggestionox.com">Suggestion Ox</a>, an anonymous employee feedback platform used by more than 450 organizations across six continents — built and run profitably with my co-founder Andrew Berkowitz, who I've been building companies with for 25 years, going back to <a href="https://www.teamsnap.com">TeamSnap</a>. I'm also a limited partner in the <a href="https://www.tweenerfund.com">Triangle Tweener Fund</a>. By night, I'm the Public Address Announcer for the NHL's <a href="https://www.nhl.com/hurricanes/">Carolina Hurricanes</a>, 2026 Stanley Cup champions, and a longtime improv comedian.
  </p>

  <p>
    The common thread is communication — whether I'm helping a team ship better software, getting 18,000 hockey fans on their feet, or teaching a room full of introverts to think on their feet through improv. I care about building things that connect people, and I'm drawn to problems where technology meets the real world.
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm based in Raleigh, North Carolina. I have a B.S. in Computer Science from the <a href="https://wm.edu/">College of William &amp; Mary</a>, and I'm active in the <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/wademinter.com">Bluesky/ATProto</a> community, where I build <a href="/software">bots, feeds, and tools</a> for the open social web.
  </p>

  <hr />

